#| "  -V, --version                Print the version and exit\n"
#| "\n"
#| "Return value:\n"
#| "-   0 No error\n"
#| "-   2 Input/Usage error\n"
#| "- %d The passphrase given does not open the secret key\n"
#| "- %d The key is protected and no passphrase was given\n"
msgid ""
"Usage: %s secret_totoken [OPTIONS]... KEY_ID|FPR\n"
"\n"
"Move PGP secrets to security token (OpenPGP smartcard).\n"
"Security token (OpenPGP smartcard) must be connected.\n"
"Output ASCII armored PGP certificate, PIN code and admin code.\n"
"\n"
"This wipes the card and takes the secret parts off this machine. Both are\n"
"final. Print the key first if it is not printed: %s secret_print.\n"
"\n"
"OPTIONS:\n"
"  -p, --passphrase PASSPHRASE  Passphrase to access secret parts of PGP key\n"
"  -P, --passfrom FILE          Get passphrase from first line of FILE (eg: fifo, tmpfs, /dev/stdin ...)\n"
"  -U, --certurl URL            URL to retrieve your PGP certificate\n"
"                               Default: https://%s/pks/lookup?op=get&search=0x<FPR>\n"
"  -L, --lang LANG              Security token (OpenPGP smartcard) prefered language (default: the locale's)\n"
"  -k, --keyserver KEYSERVER    Send PGP certificate to this public keys server\n"
"                               Empty to send it nowhere. Does not change --certurl\n"
"                               Default: %s\n"
"  -K, --pubkey FILE            Also write armored PGP certificate to given FILE\n"
"      --force                  Don't ask before resetting unempty security token (OpenPGP smartcard)\n"
"  -h, --help                   Print this help and exit\n"
"  -V, --version                Print the version and exit\n"
"\n"
"Return value:\n"
"-   0 No error\n"
"-   2 Input/Usage error\n"
"- %d The passphrase given does not open the secret key\n"
"- %d The key is protected and no passphrase was given\n"
msgstr ""
"Usage: %s totoken [OPTIONS]... KEY_ID|FPR\n"
"\n"
"Mover los secretos OpenPGP a una llave de seguridad (tarjeta OpenPGP).\n"
"La llave de seguridad (tarjeta OpenPGP) debe estar conectada.\n"
"Muestra el certificado OpenPGP en armadura ASCII, el código PIN y el código admin.\n"
"\n"
"Esto borra la tarjeta y retira las partes secretas de esta máquina. Ambas\n"
"cosas son definitivas. Imprima la clave antes si no lo está:\n"
"%s print_secret.\n"
"\n"
"OPTIONS:\n"
"  -p, --passphrase PASSPHRASE La frase que protege las partes secretas\n"
"  -P, --passfrom FILE         Leerla en la primera línea de FICHERO\n"
"  -U, --certurl URL           Dónde puede recuperarse el certificado\n"
"                              Omisión: https://%s/pks/lookup?op=get&search=0x<FPR>\n"
"  -L, --lang LANG             Idioma preferido de la tarjeta - Omisión: la locale\n"
"  -k, --keyserver KEYSERVER   Enviar el certificado a este servidor público de claves\n"
"                              Vacío para no enviarlo a ninguna parte. No cambia --certurl\n"
"                              Omisión: %s\n"
"  -K, --pubkey FILE           Escribir también el certificado con armadura ahí\n"
"      --force                 Borrar una tarjeta que no está virgen\n"
"  -h, --help                  Mostrar esta ayuda y salir\n"
"  -V, --version               Mostrar la versión y salir\n"
"\n"
"Valor de retorno:\n"
"-   0 Sin error\n"
"-   2 Error de entrada o de uso\n"
"- %d La frase de paso dada no abre la clave secreta\n"
"- %d La clave está protegida y no se dio ninguna frase de paso\n"

